WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.664
How a working team would decide.

2
00:00:01.944 --> 00:00:08.451
Start with RRF, because it needs no calibration and is a strong default with a peer-reviewed track record.

3
00:00:08.731 --> 00:00:12.976
Apply filters, including permissions, identically in both retrievers.

4
00:00:13.256 --> 00:00:20.189
Build the labeled query set from lesson 9, and measure BM25 alone, vectors alone, and the fusion.

5
00:00:20.469 --> 00:00:35.808
Then try normalized score fusion and one query technique at a time (rewriting for chat, HyDE or multi-query for vague questions), keeping each only if it beats the baseline on held-out queries by more than the noise between runs.

6
00:00:36.088 --> 00:00:42.872
Write the result down with the numbers; the next person to touch the pipeline will want to know why it is built the way it is.

7
00:00:43.152 --> 00:00:46.629
This week’s lab is exactly that experiment, run offline.
